From 3f3f891dcfc4262996f62591617fe68bb985c320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(media): align SM8750 PIX buffers to TFE address units

The gen4 TFE stores PIX image addresses and frame increments in 256-byte
units, but CAMSS currently negotiates only 16-byte row alignment. The UV
offset and either plane's frame increment can therefore be truncated for
otherwise valid NV12 dimensions. At 16x4 the UV address aliases the Y base;
at 4080x3060 it is rounded down by 192 bytes.

Require 256-byte bytesperline alignment for SM8750 PIX outputs, making
both plane offsets and frame increments exactly representable for every
supported even height. Keep RDI and the other CAMSS generations unchanged.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 32b8425b6e4..d836cc03bfc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -2362,6 +2362,10 @@ static int vfe_bpl_align_pix(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 		 */
 		ret = 0;
 		break;
+	case CAMSS_8750:
+		/* TFE image addresses and frame increments use 256-byte units. */
+		ret = 256;
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
